{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298436-let-s-talk-about-intimacies","id":1298436,"title":"Let's talk about Intimacies","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-03-21T17:39:34-07:00","id":1298436,"title":"Let's talk about Intimacies","content":"<b>Does it ever make sense to have a Tie and a Principle which are essentially the same thing?</b><br /> <br /> Can you have someone so devoted to you that they love you at the Defining level as a Tie, as well as harboring a Principle of &quot;Serve (You) In All Things&quot;?<br /> <br /> Can a being be so arrogant that they not only have a Tie of overweening self-love for themself as well as harboring a Principle of &quot;Nothing in the world is more important than me&quot;?<br /> <br /> Can someone want you dead so badly that they can have a Tie of hatred towards you as well as a Principle specifically about plotting your death as a particular form of revenge. As opposed to other forms of revenge, like ruining you completely and throwing you in jail to rot, as you once did to them?<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>How often do you or your storytellers make up Intimacies on the fly?</b><br /> <br /> I don't mean this in terms of chicanery or weaseling, but in the sense of retroactively expanding upon a character's beliefs and desires on the spur of the moment.<br /> <br /> Say that you have never once though about your character's favorite food, but as soon as someone in town bakes an apple pie, you decide that your character can apply their Minor Tie of Apple Pie (Favorite Food) on their Resolve against a bargain action that would cost you the last silver coin in your possession?<br /> <br /> Or maybe you convince your storyteller that the person you're arguing against has displayed such a strong streak of self-loathing that it counts as a Minor to Major Tie of Self-Disgust, and the storyteller agrees that's valid even if she hadn't once thought to write it down.<br /> <br /> Or perhaps appealing to the altruistic human instinct by pleading with someone (Persuade action) to the inconvenient task of finding a rope to lower into the well in which you are trapped.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T17:58:56-07:00","id":1298444,"title":"","content":"I think several of these could happen but my dividing line is this: if the devotion is intellectual or its target is abstract then its a Principle if the devotion is emotional and/or the target is a person<i> as a person</i> then its a Tie. These can certainly overlap, and one might be formed because of another, but they are distinctly different.<br /> <br /> For instance, one of the Empress' lovers and guards might have an intimacy of &quot;overwhelming loyalty&quot; both to &quot;The Scarlet Empress&quot; and &quot;The Throne of the Realm&quot;. The person might also have developed such loyalty to the Realm because they deeply loved the person in charge - but if they would lose that loyalty if the target of their affections was no longer in charge there was only a Tie and not also a Principle.<br /> <br /> As to your examples &quot;Obey this person&quot; might be a principle, though likely a poorly stated one as there is probably some other reason for the loyalty - people rarely are ideologically committed to randomly selected blind obedience. However, if it was in service to a debt, or an institutional role, or an oath of marriage then it could be a principle. The narcissist is likely also an example of both, assuming that they are ideologically committed to themselves as the Supreme Being in the Universe. Lastly, the revenge case is likely only a tie as it is just enmity toward an individual with a desire for retribution. However, if the revenge in question was related to a concept like Vendetta, or Honor-Culture it might attach to a Principle like &quot;Repay those who have wronged me or mine&quot; or &quot;Uphold my honor/the honor of my household.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23919-nabirius","name":"Nabirius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T02:19:43-07:00","id":1298554,"title":"","content":"To the first, I see no reason it couldn't be the case, but I've never really felt any great benefit to the differentiation between Ties and Principles, I know some charms care about the category of intimacy but as demonstrated it's not exactly hard for a player to reword most intimacies it to fit into the required mold. To me intimacies are just intimacies and it seems very reasonable to have multiple overlapping ones towards the same thing.<br /> <br /> To the second, all the time, sometimes it just becomes readily apparent that a character cares about something which isn't on the sheet and I don't think there's any shame to quickly scribbling it down. Sure people can game the system this way if they wanted to but then if you can't trust your playgroup not to do this then there might be other issues at play at your gaming table. I would be hesitant to try to argue an ST that another character has an intimacy not already down though, I feel it's up to them, I trust them to manage their NPCs as they trust me to manage my character and all that and I'm very edgy about player pressure on STs in general.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25050-fodor","name":"FODOR","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T02:59:01-07:00","id":1298556,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298436-let-s-talk-about-intimacies#post1298436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Does it ever make sense to have a Tie and a Principle which are essentially the same thing?</b></div> </div> </div> </div></span></span></span></div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298436-let-s-talk-about-intimacies#post1298436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Can you have someone so devoted to you that they love you at the Defining level as a Tie, as well as harboring a Principle of &quot;Serve (You) In All Things&quot;?</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Can a being be so arrogant that they not only have a Tie of overweening self-love for themself as well as harboring a Principle of &quot;Nothing in the world is more important than me&quot;?</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Can someone want you dead so badly that they can have a Tie of hatred towards you as well as a Principle specifically about plotting your death as a particular form of revenge. As opposed to other forms of revenge, like ruining you completely and throwing you in jail to rot, as you once did to them?</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Sounds about right, although it seems like it often amounts to creating a greater degree of rigidity in how one's character might act, for better or for worse.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Certainly, instilling a Principle of dedicated service sounds like the kind of thing that somebody might use another's Tie to them to empower.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FODOR</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298436-let-s-talk-about-intimacies?p=1298554#post1298554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To the first, I see no reason it couldn't be the case, but I've never really felt any great benefit to the differentiation between Ties and Principles, I know some charms care about the category of intimacy but as demonstrated it's not exactly hard for a player to reword most intimacies it to fit into the required mold. To me intimacies are just intimacies and it seems very reasonable to have multiple overlapping ones towards the same thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find the language of Ties more impactful in how they state the tangible subject that they're directed towards, and like Principles as something that get to be more abstract statements on general world view.<br /> <br /> Also, it lets Ties save on word count.<br /> <br /> Sunder's elaborating Principles seem legitimate, but I feel as though somebody trying to game the system so that their Ties qualify as Principles for the sake of Charms that will only be empowered by or safeguarding the latter is chicanery that ought to be addressed, and that there are a lot of really interesting Principles that don't readily translate in the other direction.<br /> <br /> Per Sunder's examples, there are Charms that could maintain your service to another, but an interloper would still have a means of presenting argument to reduce your esteem for the person whom you serve. Apart from making for interesting character drama, there might be times in which that has a significant impact in play; suppose a character tried using their Principle of service to bolster Resolve against a persuasion, the influence is still sufficiently compelling, and now they don't have a Tie of direct and personal love that is strong enough to function in the Decision Point anymore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T09:02:00-07:00","id":1298603,"title":"","content":"Considering you can absolutely love someone and not dedicate yourself to doing as they wish I would say absolutely yes you can have an intimacy and a principle to the same person or thing.<br /> <br /> The person with identical ties and principles to self is also contrasted nicely with opposite ties and principles directed at themself. Can make for an interesting exploration of things like depression, and duty.<br /> <br /> As to making up intimacies on the fly, absolutely. Players cant be expected to detail every aspect of thier character and I have players who struggle with the minimum intimacies at character creation. However, I wouldn't allow anything more than minor intimacies this way. If its Major it should already be directing the story and should have already been picked up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T10:18:14-07:00","id":1298642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298436-let-s-talk-about-intimacies#post1298436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Does it ever make sense to have a Tie and a Principle which are essentially the same thing?</b></div> </div> </div> </div>They are not the same thing though. A tie is something specific. Your family, the realm, dragon blooded. Specific people, nations or concepts. A principle is much more complex. It's not a specific emotion to a specific thing. If you have a principle that says you will avenge someone that gives you a much broader bonus to use compared to having a tie to get revenge on someone specific. Because a tie to someone specific does mean there are situations where it wouldn't apply.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T10:56:26-07:00","id":1298661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> As to making up intimacies on the fly, absolutely. Players cant be expected to detail every aspect of thier character and I have players who struggle with the minimum intimacies at character creation. </div> </div> </div>I think this is a very good point. It's pretty common for players to realise halfway through a game that they should probably have an intimacy to X.<br /> <br /> I would be a bit lary of people coming up with intimacies in response to social influence attempts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T11:06:34-07:00","id":1298668,"title":"","content":"As other folks have said, I believe a tie and principle may have the same subject, but cannot have the same context.<br /> <br /> As far as making up intimacies as the story progresses, I couldn't imagine not doing it this way. There's far too many ties and principles too count up everything and have it all declared beforehand. I do however allow intimacy guesses that are near the mark to work on a &quot;close emough&quot; basis.<br /> <br /> I also grant Solar XP for free when players add new intimacies according to character behaviour. Of course once its recorded they can't decrease that intimacy without corresponding behaviours, but I find there's no reason to straight jacket characters into only what's declared.<br /> <br /> Like good ole what's his (her?) name said, how can I know a thing unless I have written it down?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron-crowns.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron...dianportal.com</a> Visit Golden Shackles, Iron Crowns; a 3rd Edition Exalted Campaign ongoing since 2014","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","name":"Janissary87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2711_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T12:53:22-07:00","id":1298710,"title":"","content":"I would rather avoid Intimacies that are 100% redundant, but some overlap is probably fine.<br /> <br /> You could certainly have a Tie of hatred, along with a Principle of &quot;All slights must be avenged,&quot; and draw on both in your pursuit of vengeance against your hated enemy.<br /> <br /> A Principle about plotting a specific person's death in a specific way is...I dunno, I can't think of an objective reason why you couldn't do that. You could technically have a Principle of &quot;Nothing in life is more important than cutting Ragara Jubal's heart out with a spoon and showing it to him&quot; along with your Tie of Ragara Jubal (Hatred). I don't really like it, though. I wouldn't forbid it in all cases as ST, but playing a character who is genuinely <i>that</i> obsessive seems like it could cause a lot of trouble of the not-actually-fun variety.<br /> <br /> I have no problem with Intimacies being made up on the fly if they make sense, as long as people aren't blatantly trying to game things. I wouldn't allow a player to invent a Principle of &quot;I <i>always</i> read the fine print&quot; the very moment someone else activates Distraction of the Babbling Brook, unless the character had clearly been portrayed as behaving that way in general beforehand. (Although now that I think about it, my next character who is a bureaucrat or merchant will almost certainly have that Principle.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T14:23:03-07:00","id":1298744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298436-let-s-talk-about-intimacies?p=1298661#post1298661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would be a bit lary of people coming up with intimacies in response to social influence attempts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sometimes the subject has only come up at the time of the social influence roll, surely you remember the discussions about bodily integrity after all.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25050-fodor","name":"FODOR","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T15:33:16-07:00","id":1298767,"title":"","content":"Indeed, but I think in 3rd ed it might be dealt with better with the rules about Persuasion and the sort of things it can do.<br /> <br /> Like, you probably don't actually need an Intimacy of &quot;I don't want my hands cut off&quot; because that's a Defining Task. So you can't be persuaded to cut off your own hands except in service of a Defining Intimacy.<br /> <br /> I mean, it's not perfect; inevitably, there's going to be fringe times where you go &quot;yeah, actually in response to this social influence, it occurs to me I really should have written on an intimacy to my family, which I previously forgot&quot;. But on the other hand, if people get new intimacies every time social influence is used, it makes social-influence characters pretty weak, not to mention the charms that let you reflexively create intimacies to defend with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T16:23:52-07:00","id":1298779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298436-let-s-talk-about-intimacies?p=1298661#post1298661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think this is a very good point. It's pretty common for players to realise halfway through a game that they should probably have an intimacy to X.<br /> <br /> I would be a bit lary of people coming up with intimacies in response to social influence attempts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's kind of an issue with social influence it also appears that in this edition doesn't have perfects against mental defenses so it lags behind even more. Like it's a bit onesided and integrity is such a mixed bag it ends up pretty useless against someone using charms to persuade you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T16:38:35-07:00","id":1298781,"title":"","content":"Well, 95% of the time the perfect defence is 1 willpower, or if you have Integrity charms, 5 motes. There's some very useful effects, but as you say, it is a mixed-bag.<br /> <br /> Although I haven't seen any DB or Lunar Resolve charms used yet, so I don't know how good they are.<br /> Anyone?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 03-22-2019, 07:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T16:48:08-07:00","id":1298783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298436-let-s-talk-about-intimacies?p=1298781#post1298781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, 95% of the time the perfect defence is 1 willpower, or if you have Integrity charms, 5 motes. There's some very useful effects, but as you say, it is a mixed-bag.<br /> <br /> Although I haven't seen any DB or Lunar Resolve charms used yet, so I don't know how good they are.<br /> Anyone?</div> </div> </div> </div>Looking through them they don't seem to be as good. I guess my issue is more the fact that something like Soul-Bracing Momentous Power exists and there's pretty much nothing that can beat that kind of power. Looking at it Solar integrity has one perfect and also rightous lion stance but if you don't go against the intimacy rightous lion does nothing. However, there is nothing that can boost your resolve to even match the sheer rolling power of the combat trees.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T17:11:11-07:00","id":1298788,"title":"","content":"You can boost it by 9. It could be 15, without even a stunt. That seems like plenty.<br /> Admittedly, the charms don't really help there, but I'm not going to complain about a lack of dice tricks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T17:53:22-07:00","id":1298800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298436-let-s-talk-about-intimacies?p=1298779#post1298779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that's kind of an issue with social influence it also appears that in this edition doesn't have perfects against mental defenses so it lags behind even more.</div> </div> </div> </div>Approaching social interaction in terms of people effectively making arguments that appeal to a character's prejudices and priorities as some kind of lamentable failure state is not really taking it in the spirit that is intended, and kind of raises the question of what one thinks the value is of having a system for representing such influence in the first place is.<br /> <br /> Your &quot;perfect mental defence&quot; is not having an Intimacy sufficient to justify the task that a character would lead you towards in the first place; there's basically no magic that will override this limitation, and under the current developers there likely never will be. Even what Charms there are to interact with some kind of virtual Intimacy still tends to require some base characteristics to build off of.<br /> <br /> If a person credibly and effectively appeals to a Major or Defining Intimacy, then the difficulty of the character not being persuaded to act in that manner is rather the point; having a Defining Intimacy means a character cares about something enough that they can be willing to act in significant and dramatic manners towards that thing, whether another person's leaning on it or not. The Solar Exalted aren't really supposed to be exempt from these character dynamics.<br /> <br /> In the presence of hypothetical perfect social defences, what value do you see in having Intimacies at all?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T18:05:58-07:00","id":1298805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298436-let-s-talk-about-intimacies?p=1298800#post1298800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Approaching social interaction in terms of people effectively making arguments that appeal to a character's prejudices and priorities as some kind of lamentable failure state is not really taking it in the spirit that is intended, and kind of raises the question of what one thinks the value is of having a system for representing such influence in the first place is.<br /> <br /> Your &quot;perfect mental defence&quot; is not having an Intimacy sufficient to justify the task that a character would lead you towards in the first place; there's basically no magic that will override this limitation, and under the current developers there likely never will be. Even what Charms there are to interact with some kind of virtual Intimacy still tends to require some base characteristics to build off of.<br /> <br /> If a person credibly and effectively appeals to a Major or Defining Intimacy, then the difficulty of the character not being persuaded to act in that manner is rather the point; having a Defining Intimacy means a character cares about something enough that they can be willing to act in significant and dramatic manners towards that thing, whether another person's leaning on it or not. The Solar Exalted aren't really supposed to be exempt from these character dynamics.<br /> <br /> In the presence of hypothetical perfect social defences, what value do you see in having Intimacies at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>My problem is more towards psyche effects and the inability for you to normally defend against them; in addition, how a solar performer can just ignore the entire system in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T18:28:44-07:00","id":1298808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298436-let-s-talk-about-intimacies?p=1298805#post1298805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My problem is more towards psyche effects and the inability for you to normally defend against them</div> </div> </div> </div>Psyche effects tend to contain their own references to how they're resisted and overcome, encompassing dramatic processes for doing so. Between Excellencies and some Integrity or similar Charms, it can be possible to push oneself just far enough to make it fairly hard to lay on an effect that just can't be dealt with at the time, but for the most part the game seems to be approaching such effects as dramatic challenges to play out in the course of a story, rather than something to simply swat aside.<br /> <br /> The game doesn't actually have perfect defences at all anymore, and I feel as though it's harder to make something akin to even the best defences that combat does have function well in the slower dynamics going on in regular play. Like, a fight keeps going when a Solar drains all or most of their Initiative to stop your super high-powered attack, and you have somewhere to go and to capitalise on; what would be the similar thing that could be done in a scene of social interactions?<br /> <br /> Where overcoming a Psyche effect is expensive in Willpower, I believe the intention there is for players to be encouraged to make good use of the stunting system to play out their resistance to how they're being affected or controlled in a manner that keeps a continuous drip of Willpower back to them. It reminds me of how Holden once described the 2.5 version of Shun the Smiling Lady as something intended to encourage stories in which people struggling to not lose their love are incentivized to keep making dramatic gestures and declarations of it to continuously get the Willpower they need. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">in addition, how a solar performer can just ignore the entire system in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which parts?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T19:38:03-07:00","id":1298824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298436-let-s-talk-about-intimacies?p=1298808#post1298808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Which parts?</div> </div> </div> </div>All of it. They just have group effects that don't suffer the normal penalties and then you have things like soul-bracing which just screw the system up entirely. The solar charmset doesn't really play nice with the system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T00:32:31-07:00","id":1298876,"title":"","content":"Soul-Bracing Power does not circumvent any of the usual requirements for an influence roll, you still need sufficient supporting intimacies to get people to do what you want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8977-sigfriedmcwild","name":"sigfriedmcwild","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8977_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T01:21:03-07:00","id":1298879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298436-let-s-talk-about-intimacies?p=1298824#post1298824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They just have group effects that don't suffer the normal penalties</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems fairly standard as a thing that the Charms of anybody at all would do, and the system doesn't exactly seem strictly dependent on such a penalty.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">then you have things like soul-bracing which just screw the system up entirely.</div> </div> </div> </div>Soul-Bracing Momentous Power takes elements of the existing setting and just stretches them out a bit, and can be dependent on whether or not you place an influence that strongly contradicts a character's existing Intimacies. If it isn't an influence that contradicts a Major or Defining Intimacy, it raises the question of whether it's particularly bad for the character at all.<br /> <br /> And it's a Charm where you're gambling on how much Willpower it's going to cost with each use. It can't be sustained indefinitely, and there are probably risks to pouring your own Willpower reserves into influencing somebody else; making oneself a bit more open to being influenced in turn.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T07:20:42-07:00","id":1298946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298436-let-s-talk-about-intimacies#post1298436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Does it ever make sense to have a Tie and a Principle which are essentially the same thing?</b><br /> <br /> Can you have someone so devoted to you that they love you at the Defining level as a Tie, as well as harboring a Principle of &quot;Serve (You) In All Things&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>I could easily see one of the Bull's companions having a principle of &quot;I will serve Yurgen Kaneko to the best of my ability.&quot; as a Defining Principle, and also &quot;Love: Yurgen Kaneko.&quot; as a Minor Tie.<br /> <br /> I can then see that second one being bolstered to Defining.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24387-amayad","name":"Amayad","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}